    "title": "A standing, statewide youth-listening loop that rural towns can point to",
    "problem": "Communities get surveyed to death but rarely see results. Leaders don't know what residents actually need. Feedback loops stay broken, trust erodes.",
    "solution": "Nebraska Community Foundation and the University of Nebraska at Omaha's Center for Public Affairs Research co-created the Greater Nebraska Youth Survey in January 2020 and fielded it annually through rural school districts: over 1,000 students in 2020, 715 in five communities in 2022, 980 in 11 communities in 2023. On September 30, 2024 NCF released five-year cumulative results from 4,063 middle and high school students in 43 schools: 59% somewhat or extremely likely to live in their area as adults, 76% connected to their community, 55% naming an ideal community 'small like my hometown', 73% seeing no stigma in staying, and only 34% agreeing they play a role in their community. NCF's network is described as 270 communities and 1,500 volunteers.",
